From 6a92539f32edd98b3e4d73d97503e8684f6f278e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:06:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 43/44] Android: raytracing in the 3D viewer; STEP export
 in-process

Raytracing crashed the app: the raytracer writes its image into a pixel
unpack buffer and draws it with glDrawPixels(..., 0), and gl4es takes
that offset as a client pointer (a null dereference in glDrawPixels).
On Android the image is kept in client memory and drawn as a textured
quad in window coordinates.  gl4es lost that quad (the view stayed
black) unless another, untextured draw followed before the texture was
unbound, so one transparent pixel follows it.

STEP (and GLB, STL, ...) export from the board editor ran kicad-cli as a
child process, which an Android app can't start from its package
("execvp ... failed with error 2").  On Android the dialog now runs
EXPORTER_STEP in-process on the open board, unsaved edits included,
with the same parameters it would pass to kicad-cli (fillJob(), shared
with the job editor), and shows the exporter's messages.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
